---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Field guide"
  description="Install and explore the current Veasel Code foundation."
>
  <section class="doc-page page-grid">
    <p class="eyebrow">FIELD GUIDE / 01</p>
    <h1>
      Find your next
      <br />
      <em>good step.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A practical guide to the current Veasel Code build: set it up, understand
      what it sends, choose a provider, and follow the work that is still ahead.
    </p>
    <nav class="guide-grid" aria-label="Veasel Code guides">
      <a
        class="guide-card guide-card-featured"
        href={`${basePath}/docs/quickstart/`}
      >
        <span class="guide-card-mark">↗</span>
        <h2>Run your first session</h2>
        <p>Set up V, configure a provider, and open the terminal client.</p>
        <span class="guide-card-link">
          Quickstart <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <a class="guide-card" href={`${basePath}/docs/providers/`}>
        <span class="guide-card-mark">◌</span>
        <h2>Choose a model</h2>
        <p>Compare the provider adapters and configure credentials safely.</p>
        <span class="guide-card-link">
          Providers <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <a class="guide-card" href={`${basePath}/docs/architecture/`}>
        <span class="guide-card-mark">⌘</span>
        <h2>Understand the shape</h2>
        <p>
          Follow requests from the terminal through the V runtime and SQLite.
        </p>
        <span class="guide-card-link">
          Architecture <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <a class="guide-card" href={`${basePath}/docs/plugins/`}>
        <span class="guide-card-mark">✳</span>
        <h2>Explore Agent Plugins</h2>
        <p>
          See the v1.0.0 target and the work required for real compatibility.
        </p>
        <span class="guide-card-link">
          Compatibility <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <a class="guide-card" href={`${basePath}/docs/security/`}>
        <span class="guide-card-mark">⌂</span>
        <h2>Follow your data</h2>
        <p>
          Know what stays local, what reaches providers, and what is not
          sandboxed.
        </p>
        <span class="guide-card-link">
          Privacy and security <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <a class="guide-card" href={`${basePath}/docs/roadmap/`}>
        <span class="guide-card-mark">◎</span>
        <h2>See what comes next</h2>
        <p>Track verified foundations and the coding-agent milestones ahead.</p>
        <span class="guide-card-link">
          Roadmap <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <a class="guide-card" href={`${basePath}/docs/api/`}>
        <span class="guide-card-mark">⇄</span>
        <h2>Connect a client</h2>
        <p>Browse the loopback HTTP routes and resume server events.</p>
        <span class="guide-card-link">
          API reference <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <a class="guide-card" href={`${basePath}/docs/faq/`}>
        <span class="guide-card-mark">?</span>
        <h2>Get a clear answer</h2>
        <p>
          Check common questions about the current build and its boundaries.
        </p>
        <span class="guide-card-link">
          FAQ <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </span>
      </a>
    </nav>
    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Launch Veasel Code</h2>
      <pre><code>veasel</code></pre>
      <p>
        Download the build for your platform from the
        <a href={`${basePath}/downloads/`}>downloads page</a>. Veasel starts its
        local server when needed and opens the TUI. Press <kbd>s</kbd> on the
        home screen to configure a provider, model, endpoint, and API key. The
        server listens on <code>127.0.0.1:4097</code> by default.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Choose a model in Settings</h2>
      <pre><code>veasel</code></pre>
      <p>
        Press <kbd>s</kbd> on the home screen or enter <code>/models</code>
        in a session. Veasel saves a separate profile for each provider; local
        model presets do not need an API key by default.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="callout">
      <strong>Current boundary</strong> Provider responses stream through
      session events. Veasel can propose bounded, single-file edits; the TUI
      applies them only after you inspect the saved diff and explicitly approve
      it. Shell commands require review of the exact command, working directory,
      and timeout before approval, and run without an OS sandbox. Follow the
      implementation plan in the source repository for verified progress.
    </p>
    <p class="callout mascot-terms">
      <strong>Mascot artwork</strong> Veasel is the V language mascot. This
      pixel-art adaptation credits the V contributors and is shared under
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/">CC BY-NC 4.0</a>
      . Commercial use needs separate permission from the rights holder.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/architecture/`}>
      Next: architecture notes <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    </a>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
